      "message": "If I understand the concept, it shall be enough to have single `mUnicastGroupIdDeactivatedForBroadcastTransition` at this stage.\n\nIf Settins choose it\u0027s own group using `setActivceDevice`, this variable should be overwritten.\nWhen Settings removes it choice, we should fallback to `getEarliestConnectedDeviceGroup()` and set new `mUnicastGroupIdDeactivatedForBroadcastTransition`\n\n\nthen in all other places we should be good using mUnicastGroupIdDeactivatedForBroadcastTransition.\n\n\nFor the second step we have new API in next patch. I suggest to name it \n\n`setLeAudioPrimaryGroup()` and later we should set this into ActiveDeviceManager() - not necessary in second step.\n\nThis `setLeAudioPrimaryGroup` could still modify `mUnicastGroupIdDeactivatedForBroadcastTransition` and we could remove setting `mUnicastGroupIdDeactivatedForBroadcastTransition` in the SetActiveDevice method.\nIn case we  want to keep this User choose valid across broadcast session, then we could create `mLeAudioPrimaryGroup` variable to keep it - but this should be next patch.\n\nNext step (third one) would be to Add API to ActiveDeviceManager.setLeAudioPrimaryGroup() and let this guy to call setActiveDevice() function from LeAudioService.\nAlso, we need extend ActuveDeviceManager to be aware about start/stop broadcast source - it should be handle here: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/btservice/ActiveDeviceManager.java;l\u003d225?q\u003dActiveDeviceManager.java\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain\n\nas BluetoothProfile.LE_AUDIO_BROADCAST is missing there now.\n\nWith this, ActiveDeviceManager could properly handle all the BT devices and choose proper active device on different events. We should also then remove from LeAudioService this part: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/le_audio/LeAudioService.java;l\u003d3204?q\u003dLeAudioService.java\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain  as ActiveDeviceManager would do that.\n\n\nWith this approach, later in the future, each of the profile like A2DP or HFP, could get setPrimiary{profile}Device() which later would call ActiveDeviceManager and this guy would handle active device changes properly.\n\n\nFor this patch, just lets, try to use single `mUnicastGroupIdDeactivatedForBroadcastTransition` to track what is a",
